The app builds for testing, but the co-located XCTest bundle (`TeslaSyncTests`, which compiles EVERY
sibling surface's *Tests.swift) fails to compile on ONE pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling test file:
  TeslaSync/feature-views/SlideRenderer.FixturesTests.swift:14:16: error: static property 'echo' is
    not concurrency-safe ... a function type must be marked '@Sendable' to conform to 'Sendable'
  (committed earlier in 918982f8a "feat(apps/apple/feature-views): add SlideRenderer surface (P4)")
This file is OUTSIDE this surface's allowed scope (apps/apple/.../BatteryGaugeWidget.*), so it is not
touched here. Because it is a compile error in the shared test bundle, it blocks the whole bundle from
linking, so the on-simulator XCTest run (including this surface's 26 tests) cannot start. This surface's
tests are proven instead by the isolated SwiftPM `swift test` above (26/26 pass under Swift 6 strict
concurrency). BatteryGaugeWidget error count in the full-app compile AND the test-bundle compile: 0.
Deferred to the P99 macOS-latest acceptance gate (collision-free, sibling-fixed merged tree), exactly
as the sibling DriveScoreGaugeWidget / feature-view verifications are.

